Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• PUBLICATIONS."country_code": filter to Germany ("DE")  
• PUBLICATIONS."grant_date": select patents granted in December 2016 (20161201‑20161231)  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_date": obtain the year (YYYY) for annual filing counts  
• PUBLICATIONS."cpc": Variant column that lists all CPC symbols assigned to the publication; needs FLATTEN for one row per symbol  
• PUBLICATIONS."publication_number": quick check of sample data  
• CPC_DEFINITION."symbol": full CPC symbol; join target  
• CPC_DEFINITION."titleFull": full title/technology name to be shown in the answer  
• CPC_DEFINITION."level": restrict to level 4 groups (= 4.0)  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
• WHERE "country_code" = 'DE'  
• WHERE "grant_date" BETWEEN 20161201 AND 20161231  
• WHERE "CPC_DEFINITION"."level" = 4.0  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (LIMIT 20) that progress from simple inspection to a final solution sketch.  
